{% set actor_tags_enabled = is_audio_tags_enabled(npc.UUID) %}
{% set narrator_tags_enabled = is_audio_tags_enabled(get_narrator_uuid()) and is_narration_enabled() %}
{% set dialogue_mode = render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "transform" %}
{% set thought_mode = render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{% set has_audio_tags = actor_tags_enabled or narrator_tags_enabled %}

{% if has_audio_tags and (dialogue_mode or thought_mode) %}
  {% set tts_engine = get_actor_tts(npc.UUID) %}
  {% set useHiggsV3Tags = (tts_engine == "higgs" or tts_engine == "higgs_v3") and actor_tags_enabled %}
  {% set useChatterboxTags = tts_engine == "chatterbox" and actor_tags_enabled %}

  {% set chatterboxEmotionTags = ["[angry]", "[fear]", "[surprised]", "[whispering]", "[advertisement]", "[dramatic]", "[narration]","[happy]", "[sarcastic]"] %}
  {% set chatterboxSoundTags = ["[clear throat]","[sigh]","[shush]","[cough]","[groan]","[sniff]","[gasp]","[chuckle]","[laugh]","[crying]"] %}
  {% set allowed_audio_tags = get_allowed_audio_tags(npc.UUID) %}
  ## Voice Performance Tags
  {% if useHiggsV3Tags %}
    Use control tags `[category-tag]` to steer emotion, prosody, style, and sound effects.
  {% elif useChatterboxTags %}
    Use [square bracket tags] to direct vocal performance. Tags control emotion, delivery, and reactions—the AI voice interprets them contextually.
  {% else %}
    Use free-form natural language [square bracket tags] to direct vocal performance. Place them before the text they apply to.
  {% endif %}
  
  {% if useHiggsV3Tags %}
    {% set originalEmotionsTags = ["emotion-affection", "emotion-amusement", "emotion-anger", "emotion-arousal", "emotion-awe", "emotion-bitterness", "emotion-confusion", "emotion-contemplation", "emotion-contentment", "emotion-determination", "emotion-disgust", "emotion-elation", "emotion-enthusiasm", "emotion-fear", "emotion-helplessness", "emotion-longing", "emotion-pride", "emotion-relief", "emotion-sadness", "emotion-shame", "emotion-surprise"] %}
    {% set originalStylesTags = ["style-singing", "style-shouting", "style-whispering"] %}
    {% set originalProsodyTags = ["prosody-speed_very_slow", "prosody-speed_slow", "prosody-speed_fast", "prosody-speed_very_fast", "prosody-pitch_low", "prosody-pitch_high", "prosody-expressive_high", "prosody-expressive_low"] %}
    {% set originalSfxTags = ["sfx-cough", "sfx-laughter", "sfx-crying", "sfx-screaming", "sfx-burping", "sfx-humming", "sfx-sigh", "sfx-sniff", "sfx-sneeze"] %}
    {% set filteredEmotionsTags = "" %}
    {% set filteredStylesTags = "" %}
    {% set filteredProsodyTags = "" %}
    {% set filteredSfxTags = "" %}

    {% for tag in allowed_audio_tags %}
      {% if tag in originalEmotionsTags %}
        {% set filteredEmotionsTags = filteredEmotionsTags + "`["+tag+"]`," %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if tag in originalStylesTags %}
        {% set filteredStylesTags = filteredStylesTags + "`["+tag+"]`," %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if tag in originalProsodyTags %}
        {% set filteredProsodyTags = filteredProsodyTags + "`["+tag+"]`," %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if tag in originalSfxTags %}
        {% set filteredSfxTags = filteredSfxTags + "`["+tag+"]`," %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

    {% set exampleTag1 = "[sfx-sigh]Haah," %}
    {% set exampleTag2 = "[emotion-elation]" %}
    {% set exampleTag3 = "[style-whispering]" %}
    {% set exampleTag4 = "[prosody-pitch_low]" %}

    **Format:** `[category-tag]`, glued to text with no space. Only use tags from the catalog below — anything else degrades audio or gets read aloud literally. These are audio-only; never mix them with non-audio markup like `<internal_thought>`.

    **Placement**
    - **Sentence-level** (emotion, style, prosody `speed_*`/`pitch_*`/`expressive_*`): at the **very start** of the sentence — colors the whole sentence, so tag it once, not repeatedly.
    - **Inline sfx**: at the exact spot the sound occurs, glued to a short onomatopoeia. e.g. `[sfx-cough]Ahem, let's begin.`
    
    **Stacking:** Combine at most **one tag per category** at a sentence start (e.g. emotion + style, or emotion + a prosody tag) — they control different things. Never stack two from the *same* category. Inline `sfx` can be added on top anywhere.

    **Bare onomatopoeia needs no tag.** "Ohh", "Mmh", "Ugh", "Aah" can sit directly in the line as light texture. Use the `sfx` tag only when you want a distinct, emphasized beat.

    
    **Tag catalog (41 total):**
    - **Emotions:** {{filteredEmotionsTags}}
    - **Styles:** {{filteredStylesTags}}
    - **Prosody:** {{filteredProsodyTags}}
    - **SFX (inline, glued to onomatopoeia):** {{filteredSfxTags}}

    **Examples**
    - `[emotion-arousal][prosody-pitch_low]Come closer... I have a secret.`
    - `[emotion-elation][sfx-laughter]Haha, welcome, welcome!`
    - `You want the truth? [emotion-bitterness]Fine. He was never coming back.`
    - `[emotion-anger][emotion-disgust]...` ❌ two emotions — pick one.
  {% elif useChatterboxTags %}
    {% set exampleTag1 = "[sigh]" %}
    {% set exampleTag2 = "[happy]" %}
    {% set exampleTag3 = "[whispering]" %}
    {% set exampleTag4 = "[dramatic]" %}
    **Allowed emotion tags (OPTIONAL, at the beginning of emotional sentence):**
    {{join(chatterboxEmotionTags, ", ")}}
    **Allowed sound tags (OPTIONAL, may appear ANYWHERE):**
    {{ join(chatterboxSoundTags, ", ") }}
    **How to write each dialogue/thought line**
    - You MAY start the line with ONE emotion tag, but it is optional.
    - You MAY insert multiple sound tags anywhere in the line (start, middle, end).
    - Sound tags must be standalone tokens (surrounded by spaces or punctuation), not attached to words.
    - Do NOT invent other bracketed text. Only use the allowed tags above.
    - Keep tags meaningful; don’t spam them (typically 0–3 sound tags per line unless the scene demands it).
    
    **Examples**
    - [whispering] Keep your voice down - [shush] - they’ll hear us. [sigh]
    - I told you not to touch that - [groan] - ever again. [cough]
    - [happy] [clear throat] So… we agree? [chuckle] Great.
  {% else %}
    - Start with a vocal verb (say/sound/shout/whisper/sing...) then describe the delivery—emotion, volume, pitch, pace, texture, vocal style—not internal feelings.
    - Combine multiple vocal qualities in single [square bracket instruction] for nuanced delivery. Be specific and concrete.
    - Emphasize words by CAPITALIZING them.
    - **Inline non-verbal reactions (These are not free-form tags and must be used exactly as written):** [laugh], [sigh], [clear throat], [breathe], [cough], [yawn]
  {% endif %}
  {% if not useHiggsV3Tags and not useChatterboxTags and actor_tags_enabled %}
  **Examples**: 
    ❌ [internally amused, grunt softly] → ❌ vague internal feeling + invented non-verbal, not vocal delivery
    ✅ [say cautiously with deliberate pauses in a low voice] I suppose you're right.
    ✅ [whisper in a hushed style] I've never seen such a majestic creature. [laugh] It's incredible!
    ✅ [sing joyfully] Because FUN adventures are the ones with you!
  {% endif %}
  {% if not actor_tags_enabled and narrator_tags_enabled %}
    Tags only work in *narration*, not dialogue.
  {% endif %}
  {% if actor_tags_enabled and not narrator_tags_enabled and is_narration_enabled() %}
    Tags only work in dialogue, not *narration*.
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}